# Production content: exercise titles, and specs whose feedback messages teachers wrote.
# This repo is public, so the export and everything derived from it stays local.
#
# **Deny everything, then name what may be committed.** This file used to list the output shapes it
# expected — deliberately broader than the docs' own examples, and still a list. Its sibling in
# `../adoc-to-md/` was written the same way and lost on 2026-08-31: a run wrote `payload.json` where
# the rule said `payload.jsonl`, and several hundred real exercises sat untracked in a public
# repository until someone happened to look. The same near-miss was available here.
#
# An allowlist cannot lose that way. A script inventing a new output name is ignored by default, and
# the cost is that adding a tracked file means adding a line — the rare case, and the deliberate one.
*

!.gitignore
!README.md
!RUNBOOK.md
!*.py
!*.sql
